==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|fore|ground|lang=en}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|voorgrond||foreground}}, German {{m|de|Vordergrund||foreground}}, Danish {{m|da|forgrund||foreground}}, Swedish {{m|sv|förgrund||foreground}}, Norwegian {{m|no|forgrunn||foreground}}, Icelandic {{m|is|forgrunni||foreground}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈfɔː(ɹ)ˌɡɹaʊnd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-foreground.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The elements of an image which lie closest to the [[picture plane]].
# The subject of an image, often depicted at the bottom in a [[two-dimensional]] work.
# {{lb|en|computing}} the [[application]] the user is currently interacting with; the application window that appears in front of all others.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|background}}
* {{l|en|midground}}

